EVT2004 TEXT x.Workspace.Consoles.ElectricGridConsole.DRMScreen.SurfaceGui.MainFrame.MainframeFrame.OperationsFrame.TextLabel <b>Gateway Transporters, Medical dispensers, and especially the control room consoles will be non-functional</b> if there are too few QPUs or the mainframe completely shuts down.
EVT2005 TEXT x.Workspace.Consoles.ElectricGridConsole.DRMScreen.SurfaceGui.MainFrame.MainframeFrame.OperationsFrame.TextLabel Large stockpiles of QPUs tend to be counterintuitive, so operators <b>may have to use a Synthesiser Unit</b> in order to sucessfully replace dying QPUs. Be weary that the mainframe is always kept at extremely low temperatures, and as such haste is of the essence. {wip system}
EVT2006 TEXT x.Workspace.Consoles.ElectricGridConsole.DRMScreen.SurfaceGui.MainFrame.MainframeFrame.OperationsFrame.TextLabel Operators are required to <b>replace</b> the affected QPU <b>as soon as possible</b>, otherwise machines across the facility will begin to shut off in order to conserve resources.
